+---
+"@beep/libpff": patch
+---
+
+Deepen the pffexport engine into the real PST export driver (file-processing-capability P3): probe `pffexport -V` once (bounded) at construction onto `descriptor.version`, derive per-message `message.eml` children (`message/rfc822`) via a byte-preserving splice that rewrites the MIME-structural headers to describe the decoded body, write per-tree `messages.jsonl` relationship manifests of `LibpffMessageRecord` rows preserving folder/message/attachment links (including nested attached messages), apply the new `existingExportPolicy` (`fail`/`replace`) across all pffexport target trees (`.export`/`.orphans`/`.recovered`) and collect children from every produced tree, and add an opt-in `BEEP_TEST_PST_PATH` live integration lane with the EDRM Enron public PST sample documented as the fixture fallback.
